  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x & =7+2\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}\u2061x & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=-\\frac{3}{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-\\frac{3}{7})=(-25.376\\,933\u2026)^{\u2218}\u2248-{25.377}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add ${360}^{\u2218}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-{25.377}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}={334.623}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSo,  our first solution is ${x}_{1}={334.623}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={25.377}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={25.377}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062614/assets/2358d2c829f52ba8727afc10a609f923ca441bb55dc398cda78c619454f6eac5.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{\u2218}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}+{25.377}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={205.377}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx\u2248{205}^{\u2218},\\,x\u2248{335}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
